    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for a `checkDigit` field = a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. Following the project's established pattern for derived owner fields (`membershipNumber`, `locality`, etc. \u2014 `@Transient` getters on `Owner` auto-mapped by MapStruct into the generated `OwnerDto`), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getCheckDigit()` that scans `customerCode` right-to-left, doubling the rightmost digit first, skipping non-digits, and returns `(10 - sum % 10) % 10` (the standard Luhn check digit, matching the test's `luhn(...)` reference exactly). Returns `null` when `customerCode` is absent, consistent with `getMembershipNumber()`.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` read-only integer (0\u20139) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct wires `getCheckDigit()` \u2192 `checkDigit` into the JSON response.\n\nNo new function step or DB column was needed \u2014 `checkDigit` is purely derived from the already-stored `customerCode`, so it resolves correctly on both the POST create response and subsequent GET reads.\n\n`coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` and the full test suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
