    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `getCheckDigit()` slots naturally into Owner.java's established idiom for derived values. The file already hosts a family of `@Transient` computed getters (`getDisplayName`, `getInitials`, `getMembershipNumber`, `getMembershipLevel`) that each:\n\n- carry a Javadoc describing the derivation and null-behavior,\n- null-guard on absent source fields, and\n- inline their computation directly rather than delegating to a helper/utility.\n\n`getCheckDigit()` matches all three conventions exactly, and is placed right beside the other `customerCode`-derived getter (`getMembershipNumber`), so a maintainer would find it where they'd expect. The Luhn logic is a single self-contained algorithm living on the entity that owns the source field \u2014 the right unit, not duplicated anywhere, and consistent in style with `getMembershipLevel`'s inline branching. There's no existing Luhn/check-digit utility it should have reused, and extracting a ~15-line private helper would actually diverge from the surrounding inline style.\n\nThe OpenAPI addition mirrors the adjacent `customerCode` property entry (title/description/`readOnly`, plus appropriate `integer`/`int32` with `minimum`/`maximum` bounds matching a single digit). Additive and coherent.",
